        "iopath_ifnone_edge_modpath": {
          "count": 144,
          "reason": "The cell's own Verilog model declares this arc only through 'ifnone' edge-sensitive module paths (e.g. 'ifnone (posedge A1 => (Z:A1))', the shape gf180mcu models give XOR/XNOR inputs and MUX selects), which Icarus Verilog does not support: it discards every such path at elaboration ('sorry: ifnone with an edge-sensitive path is not supported'), so no IOPATH entry -- unqualified or edge-qualified -- can match it ('Unable to match ModPath'). Those IOPATH entries were removed before annotation and counted here, and 'arcs' names every affected cell arc. Removing them cannot change simulated timing relative to annotating them, but the listed arcs simulate with NO module-path delay at all (neither the SDF's nor the model's placeholder): their characterised cell delay is not represented in this run. An IOPATH that fails to match any other arc is left in place and still fails loudly",
